The park is very full on Saturday afternoon.
The weather is wonderfully warm.
Many people are walking here in the sun.
Bruno sees many other dogs.
He is very curious and sniffs everywhere.
I hold the lead firmly.
Suddenly something moves in the grass.
A squirrel runs quickly to a tree.
Bruno sees it immediately.
He wants to run into the bushes right away!
He pulls hard on the lead.
I pull him back quickly.
"Stop!", I call loudly.
"Stay here, Bruno!"
He looks at me and stands still.
I think of Sabine's strict rule.
Bruno is not allowed to run around freely.
I stroke him briefly as a reward.
Then we stroll on comfortably.
